version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
abstract: >
  TR-FactBench is a 4-class source-grounded factuality verification benchmark
  for Turkish. It covers three domains (finance, legal, medical) with 4,800
  training, 960 general dev, and 600 stress-test examples, and a held-out
  set of 480 examples (120 source contexts) labeled independently by two
  annotators and adjudicated (Cohen's kappa 0.867). The benchmark evaluates
  fine-tuned Turkish encoder models (including ELECTRA and ModernBERT) and four
  zero-shot/few-shot LLM baselines. Code is released under MIT; project-created
  questions, claims, labels, and metadata under CC BY 4.0.

keywords:
  - Turkish NLP
  - factuality verification
  - hallucination detection
  - natural language inference
  - LoRA
  - ELECTRA
